#
# THIS FIXTURE PROVES DRIFT DETECTION ONLY, NEVER CORRECTNESS. It records the
# accepted (time, step) sequence a past build chose; it cannot tell you that
# sequence was right, and it will freeze a defect just as faithfully as a fix.
#
# Re-baseline protocol -- all four steps, in order:
#   1. Name the code change that moved the sequence. "It moved" is a regression.
#   2. Produce oracle evidence that the deck's waveforms are still correct
#      (ngspice/Xyce comparison, or .MEAS-checked expectations). Agreement with
#      the new sequence itself is not evidence.
#   3. Regenerate with RSPICE_BLESS_TIMESTEP_GOLDENS=1 cargo test -p rspice-core
#      --test timestep_sequence_goldens (the bless run fails on purpose).
#   4. Commit the fixtures alone, with a message stating the cause of the change
#      and citing the oracle evidence from step 2.
#
